A51 GPU: Mali-G72 probe and power (bsd/dev/a51_gpu.c).

First part of the GPU service (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-29-a51-gpu-
kernel-service-design.md), ported from the Galaxy S7's HeroGPU. A thread
started from IOFindBSDRoot waits 5 s, then reads the GPU at 0x11500000 only
if the PMU G3D domain (0x11860000 + 0x4064) reports on, logs its identity
("A51 GPU: id ..."), and at a51gpu=2 soft-resets it and powers L2, all
shader cores and the tiler ("A51 GPU: ready ..."). a51gpu=0 does nothing;
a51gpu_pretend_off=1 exercises the domain-off path. No configuration
quirks (Linux Panfrost writes none for the G72). a51_gpu_mmu.h (page-table
and VA helpers, host-tested in tools/a51/gpu) is shipped for the next patch.

